# The policy set AND the required-check enforcement surface, owned by the
# repository owner (decision 0009 as amended 2026-09-16; #201 comments
# 5702359298 and 5702401684).
#
# GitHub reads this file for two things. It auto-requests the owner's review on
# a pull request touching a path below, unless the owner authored it. And
# `main-protect`'s `pull_request` rule carries `require_code_owner_review` (0009
# step 6, 2026-09-17), so such a pull request cannot merge without the owner's
# approving review on GitHub, which is how the owner approves a policy change.
#
# The owner is @tvofi and not the approver App: GitHub's docs list users and
# teams with explicit write access as code owners and name no App form. Every
# other path has no code owner, and the App's approving review serves those.
# docs/HANDOVER.md is deliberately absent: it carries state, not rules.
# Apps are never code owners — neither the approver nor the author App can
# satisfy an owner review; only @tvofi can (decision 0011).
#
# THE REQUIRED-CHECK ENFORCEMENT SURFACE (R6-D11-01, #1402). The tracked files
# that produce or implement the checks `main-protect-checks` requires carried no
# owner, so `require_code_owner_review` could not demand the owner for a change
# to the checks themselves. The surface is DERIVED, never carried: the six
# `.github/workflows/*.yml`, the scripts their non-comment lines execute, the
# hooks, and their wiring. Re-derive it with
# `python3 tools/audit/round6/D11/fix/codeowners_gap.py`, which prints the
# surface size and how many of its files an owner-carrying pattern matches:
# against the pre-#1402 file that second count is zero, against this one it is
# the surface size. A new check script is owned only once it is added below or
# matched by one of these patterns — re-run the harness and extend this block
# when the surface moves.
#
# Nothing in the test gate opens this file (tests/closure.py lists it INERT).

/CLAUDE.md                                @tvofi
/AGENTS.md                                @tvofi
/.claude/rules/                           @tvofi
/.cursor/rules/                           @tvofi
/.claude/skills/steward/SKILL.md          @tvofi
/.claude/workflows/web-fragments.md       @tvofi
/tools/audit/briefs/                      @tvofi
# COMMON.md is the finder's contract and is not policy (CLAUDE.md says so);
# a later line with a path and no owner un-owns it, because the last matching
# pattern wins.
/tools/audit/briefs/COMMON.md
/tools/audit/README.md                    @tvofi
/tools/audit/harnesses/README.md          @tvofi
/tests/README.md                          @tvofi
/docs/decisions/                          @tvofi
/.github/PULL_REQUEST_TEMPLATE.md         @tvofi
/.github/CODEOWNERS                       @tvofi

# --- The required-check enforcement surface (R6-D11-01, #1402). ---
# The workflow files that hold the jobs whose status contexts the ruleset
# requires. The whole directory: every file here is a workflow on `main`.
/.github/workflows/                       @tvofi
# The hooks that run in every seat's session, and the wiring that gives a
# session its hooks. `always-fails.sh` is a deliberately unwired control; the
# whole directory is the surface.
/.claude/hooks/                           @tvofi
/.claude/settings.json                    @tvofi
# The governance scripts the required-check jobs execute. Enumerated, not
# `/.claude/workflows/`: that directory is mostly fixtures, and owning it
# wholesale would put a review on every fixture edit.
